<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1    This Statement has been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on May 18, 2019.  n2     The Statement has been prepared in accordance with the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 (Ind AS) prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 and other recognised accounting practices and policies to the extent applicable.   n3     The Company is engaged in the business of  High Energy Materials  and has only one reportable segment in accordance with Ind AS 108  Operating Segment .  n4     Post the applicability of Goods and service Tax (GST) with effect from July 01,2017, revenue from operations is disclosed net of GST. Revenue from operations till June 30, 2017 is inclusive of Excise Duty. For comparison, Revenue from operations have been disclosed on Gross as well as Net basis.  n5     Securities Allotment Committee of the company, at its meeting held on January 25, 2019, has approved the allotment of 1,15,100 (1,00,100 to promoters and 15,000 to others) equity shares of face value of Rs. 10/- each against conversion of equal number of warrants on payment of the balance 75% of the issue price of Rs.408 per equity share (including a premium of Rs. 398 per equity share), with the balance amount received aggregating to Rs.3,52,20,600.  nSecurities Allotment Committee of the company, at its meeting held on 25 January 2019, has approved the allotment of 1,15,100 (1,00,100 to promoters and 15,000 to others) equity shares of face value of Rs. 10/- each against conversion of equal number of warrants on payment of the balance 75% of the issue price, at issue price of Rs. 408 per equity share (including a premium of Rs. 398 per equity share), with the balance amount received aggregating to Rs.3,52,20,600.  nThe company has forfeited 20,000 warrants as the warrant-holders, who have paid Rs.20,40,000 (being 25% of issue price), did not pay the balance 75% against the said warrants.   n6     The Board of Directors has recommended a dividend of Rs. 2.70 per Equity Share of Rs. 10/- each for the year 2018-19 subject to the approval of shareholders at the ensuing Annual General Meeting of the Company.  n7     The Figures for the quarter ended March 31, 2019 and March 31, 2018 are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of full financial year and the published year to date unaudited figures up to the third quarter of the current and previous financial years i.e., 2018-19 and 2017-18 respectively.  n8     Figures for the previous year / periods have been regrouped, wherever necessary, to conform to the current year / periods classification. </in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
